    "publisher": "Government of India — Ministry of Finance / Ministry of Labour & Employment; State Governments of Karnataka, Maharashtra, Tamil Nadu, Telangana, West Bengal",
    "document_reference": "IT Act §115BAC/§16(ia)/§87A Finance Act 2025; EPF Act §6 Scheme para 26A; ESI Act 1948; PT Acts KA-1976, MH-1975, TN-1992, TG-AP adapted, WB-1979",
    "url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/1362",
    "retrieved_on": "2026-03-31",
    "notes": "Rates transcribed for monthly payroll (annual slab/12). §115BAC new-regime slabs (annual): 0-4L 0%, 4-8L 5%, 8-12L 10%, 12-16L 15%, 16-20L 20%, 20-24L 25%, >24L 30%. Monthly bounds: 33333.33 / 66666.67 / 100000 / 133333.33 / 166666.67 / 200000 / open. Standard deduction §16(ia) ₹75,000/yr → ₹6,250/mo subtracted before banding. §87A rebate ₹60,000/yr → ₹5,000/mo, income limit ₹12,00,000/yr → ₹1,00,000/mo taxable; marginal relief above ₹12L is NOT encoded — verifier must decide whether v1.1 needs it (checklist). Cess 4% is applied on net tax after rebate as per Finance Act 2025; the pack's tax_bands rates are the slab rates before cess, cess is a separate 4% on the computed tax (engine applies as surcharge). EPF: 12% employee + 12% employer on wage ceiling ₹15,000 (15000) (EPF Scheme para 26A caps contribution base); employer 12% is EPS/EPF-split in law (8.33% EPS up to ₹15,000 (15000) + remainder EPF) — v1 records 12% flat (checklist for verifier). ESI: 0.75% employee / 3.25% employer, coverage limit ₹21,000 (21000) (ESI Act — contributions skipped above limit, not capped). PT tables reuse schedule entry's `rate` field as flat monthly amount (qs per contract § slice 2). Thresholds/overtime null where India sets no value; Factories Act limits not encoded. Gratuity explicitly excluded — Payment of Gratuity Act 1972 deferred to a later slice (no accrual in v1). Single salary field means PF/ESI base = full gross (Basic+DA simplification) — checklist. MH Feb ₹300/cap ₹2500 (2500) not encoded — checklist. TN statutory schedule is half-yearly with intermediate slabs — v1 uses single ₹208.50 above ₹25,000 (checklist). WB rows transcribed; verifier must confirm all 10 rows (checklist)."
  },
